WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:11.600
A Progress Reward Model (PRM) scores how far a task has come at every step.

2
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:17.600
It serves as a dense reward, a verifier of each step, and a monitor of the execution.

3
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.000
In long tasks, the current frame often cannot tell how far the task has come.

4
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.000
State Recall: which mat did this block come from? That fact left the frame long ago.

5
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:29.200
Sequence Tracking: is the leftmost block done? The order is not visible in one frame.

6
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:34.600
Recurrence Disambiguation: just before and after a placement, the frames look the same.

7
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:40.400
We run five PRMs with the same input format, once without and once with the right context.

8
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:50.600
Every one of them cuts its progress error by 77% to 82%.

9
00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:56.600
PRMs are not blind but lost: they need to be told where in the task they are.

10
00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:03.400
ProgressCompass keeps the PRM frozen and lets general-purpose VLMs supply the context.

11
00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:10.000
An Orienter states the step, the PRM scores it, and a Verifier checks that it is done.

12
00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:16.600
A text-only Navigator runs the loop and carries the verified plan from step to step.

13
00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:24.600
Wrapped in the loop, the same frozen RoboMeter cuts its error from 25.4 to 9.3.

14
00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:32.600
Its curves follow the ground truth where the frozen model drifts, stalls, or falls back.

15
00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:39.000
It stays robust when the video stops early, does more than asked, or follows an unrelated task.

16
00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:46.600
Parallelizing the loop cuts wall-clock time by 65.6%, keeping the cost of the added components low.

17
00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:54.500
ProgressCompass: embodied progress reward models, reoriented with the right context.

